      "description": "Watch Newells Old Boys vs Talleres Cordoba highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 25, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina clash between Newell's Old Boys and Talleres Cordoba on July 25, 2026, delivered a tactical battle defined by grit and narrow margins. Both sides entered the pitch looking to assert dominance, resulting in a match that hinged on disciplinary discipline and a single clinical moment from the penalty spot. Tactical Stalemate in the Opening Half The first half was a display of defensive organization as both teams struggled to find clear-cut chance opportunities. The intensity was palpable from the start, and the referee was forced to reach for his pocket as early as the 15th minute when Roman Riquelme received a yellow card for a mistimed challenge. While Newell's Old Boys attempted to control possession, Talleres remained compact, ensuring that the primary narrative of the opening 45 minutes was one of midfield duels rather than goalmouth action. The sides went into the break level after a brief period of stoppage time. Coccaro Breaks the Deadlock The second half saw immediate tactical adjustments, with Talleres introducing Augusto Schott to bolster their flanks. However, the momentum shifted decisively in favor of the hosts in the 55th minute. After a foul in the box, the referee pointed to the spot, giving Newell's a golden opportunity. Matias Coccaro stepped up and coolly converted the penalty, sending the home fans into raptures. Following the goal , Talleres responded with a double substitution, bringing on Valentin Depietri and Rick to inject pace into their attack. Late Red Card and Final Whistle As the game entered its final stages, the pressure began to take its toll on the players' discipline. In the 86th minute, the match took another dramatic turn when Roman Riquelme was shown his second yellow card, resulting in a red card and an early exit for the player . Down to ten men, Talleres struggled to mount a cohesive comeback despite a lengthy nine minutes of added time. Newell's Old Boys managed the closing moments with experience, successfully defending their lead until the referee blew the final whistle to end a physical sports contest."
